WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.250
- [Instructor] We are told
Liam multiplies two numbers

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:05.756
and gets an even product.

00:00:05.756 --> 00:00:09.330
What could be true about
the numbers Liam multiplied?

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:11.140
It says Choose 2 answers.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:13.340
So pause this video and
see if you can figure out

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:16.580
which two of these could be true.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:18.410
All right, now let's do this together.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.460
And we have to think
about what could be true.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:21.800
They don't have to be true.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:23.641
It just has to be possible.

00:00:23.641 --> 00:00:27.107
Okay, now is it possible
that both numbers were even?

00:00:27.107 --> 00:00:32.107
Can you multiply two even
numbers and get an even product?

00:00:32.453 --> 00:00:33.330
Well, sure.

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:35.580
And I can imagine examples
that get us there.

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:39.690
If you multiply two times
four, which is equal to eight,

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:43.240
you have an even times an
even that gets you an even.

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:46.700
In fact, in general, when you
multiply two evens together,

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:49.140
you will get an even product.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:54.140
And so this is definitely,
this definitely could be true.

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:57.057
Both numbers were odd.

00:00:57.057 --> 00:01:00.400
You might remember that
an odd times an odd

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.338
is always going to be an odd,

00:01:02.338 --> 00:01:04.850
or you could look at a few examples

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:07.210
and feel pretty confident
that that's the case.

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:11.930
If you multiply three times
five, that's equal to 15.

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:14.485
Odd times odd is equal to an odd number.

00:01:14.485 --> 00:01:19.485
If you multiply seven
times nine, you get 63.

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:23.830
Once again, odd times odd is equal to odd.

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:27.027
So there's no way that you
can multiply two odd numbers

00:01:27.027 --> 00:01:29.640
and get an even product.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:31.680
So we would rule this out.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:35.743
One number was even
and one number was odd.

00:01:35.743 --> 00:01:37.330
Well, let's think about what happens

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.019
when you multiply an even times an odd.

00:01:40.019 --> 00:01:44.225
If I multiply two times
three, that's equal to six.

00:01:44.225 --> 00:01:47.480
So you have an even,
I'll just put an e there,

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:50.879
times an odd, is equal to an even.

00:01:50.879 --> 00:01:54.500
And so the two ways that
you can get an even product

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:56.948
is either if you're multiplying
an even times an even

00:01:56.948 --> 00:02:00.510
or an even times an odd.

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:04.130
Essentially, an even times
either an even or an odd

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:06.260
is going to give you an even product.

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:07.623
Let's do another example.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:11.640
We're asked which of the
following have an even product?

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:13.450
It says, once again, Choose 2 answers.

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:14.650
So pause this video again,

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:16.300
and see if you can figure it out.

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:19.602
Okay, 8 fives.

00:02:19.602 --> 00:02:24.600
So 8 fives is the same
thing as eight times five,

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:27.320
and this is a situation where
we're multiplying an even,

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:30.730
e for even, times an odd, which
we've already talked about

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:34.600
is going to give us an even
result, an even product.

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:37.370
You don't even have to know
that eight times five is 40,

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:38.550
which is an even number.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:41.320
We have an even times an odd,

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.270
which is going to give us an even product.

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:46.370
So this will definitely
give us an even product.

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:49.770
An odd number times an even number.

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:51.070
Well, we've already talked about that.

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:54.530
Any even, odd, or an even times an even

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:56.470
is going to give you an even product.

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:59.150
So we can fill that one in.

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:02.640
And then five times three,
you have an odd times an odd,

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.570
which is going to give you an odd number.

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:07.020
Even if you didn't know
that this is going to be 15,

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.630
you would know that an odd times an odd

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:10.460
is always going to give
you an odd product,

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:11.630
not an even product.

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:13.413
So we would pick these first two.

